  "change": {
    "behavior": "Format a numeric index into a stack buffer and look up an existing atom for descriptor queries, deletion, and inherited-accessor checks. If an ordinary array receives an unowned index whose canonical atom is absent and whose prototype chain contains no Proxy or TypedArray, write directly to the array's authoritative element storage. Existing generic paths remain for interned keys, descriptors, non-extensible receivers, proxies, typed arrays, and other cases.",
    "representation": "The existing atom table remains the authority for whether a string-keyed property can exist. No per-array flag, duplicate descriptor index, or new index map was added. Query-only operations do not grow the atom table.",
    "binding_time": "The canonical decimal index is formatted on the stack; atom-table presence is checked at access time. An absent atom proves no ordinary string-keyed descriptor for that index has been installed. Proxy and TypedArray prototype chains retain the generic path.",
    "review_note": "The `numeric.rs` diff updates test helper calls to the existing rewrite-rule parameters; it does not alter production code."
  },
